// ROLE admits exactly five promises: inert, navigate, reversible,
// irreversible, proposal. Each is a claim about what happens when the operator
// acts, and none of them names a widget.
//
// 'destructive' is the word Rule 79 uses for the ACT, and it is deliberately
// not a role: the law splits that class in two -- reversible, where one-click
// undo is owed, and irreversible, where confirmation is reserved. A single
// 'destructive' role would collapse the distinction the rule exists to make.
//
// Expected: UNKNOWN_ROLE

DEFINE INTERACTION archive_invoice (
  SATISFIES [ACT],
  ALWAYS_REACHABLE [UNDO],
  ROLE destructive
)
